Cat command

Synatx: cat <file-name>

Above will diplay the content of the file on the terminal

cat -n <file-name>

Above command will display the content of the file on the terminal along with line numbers

cat -b <file-name>


Above command will display the content of the file on the terminal along with line numbers where the content is present

cat -s <file-name>

Above command will display the content of the file on the terminal by supressing multiple empty lines into sinle empty line

cat -n -s <file-name>

Above command will display the content of the file on the terminal by supressing multiple empty lines into sinle empty line
and also it will add the line numbers

cat <file1.txt> <file2.txt> <file3.txt>
It will display the content of files file1.txt,file2.txt and file3.txt on the terminal

